[LEARNING PROJECT]

plank :- intrigrate btrfs snapshot to systemd-boot

it does few things like following:

- Creates bootloader entries for discovered snapshots.
- Deletes loader entries that no longer point to an actual snapshot
  or kernel.
- Lists and displays individual bootloader entries created by Plank.
- Checks for kernel mismatches (see docs/kernelmismatch.txt).
- Lists subvolumes for a given Btrfs filesystem along with additional
  information.
- Provides a tree view of Btrfs filesystem subvolumes, making it 
  easy to see parent and child relationships.

This project is currently in the development phase and includes many
non-traditional ways of doing things (as I am still learning), along 
with inevitable bugs.

